M_Pl -> 1 TeV: 16.09 decades, L = 37.04

== (a1) QED with N_f unit-charge Dirac fermions; alpha(1 TeV) = 1/128 ==
   singlet (all fermions vs photon): d delta/d ln mu = ((2N_f+4)/3)(alpha/pi) delta ; nonsinglet (fermion vs fermion): (4/3)(alpha/pi)
  N_f = 1: 1/alpha(M_Pl) =  120.1;  suppression M_Pl->TeV: singlet 0.827, nonsinglet 0.881
  N_f = 3: 1/alpha(M_Pl) =  104.4;  suppression M_Pl->TeV: singlet 0.712, nonsinglet 0.873
  N_f = 8: 1/alpha(M_Pl) =   65.1;  suppression M_Pl->TeV: singlet 0.430, nonsinglet 0.845
  (N_f = 1 to m_e instead of TeV, F2's b=1 guess gave 0.887; b = 2 derived here gives 0.787 at fixed alpha = 1/137)

== (a2) QCD: gluon + n_f = 6 quark flavours (same speed), alpha_s(1 TeV) = 0.0885 ==
  singlet rate = 3.778 alpha_s/pi ; alpha_s(M_Pl) = 0.0190 ; S = (alpha_P/alpha_T)^1.079 = 0.190
  nonsinglet (quark vs quark): S = (alpha_P/alpha_T)^0.508 = 0.458

