  GNY in d=4 (eps=0): marginal -> logs only                                z = 0.0000: factor over 16.1 decades = 1.00e+00
  QED3 large N, nonsinglet, N=4 two-comp (64/(5 pi^2 N), derived)          z = 0.3242: factor over 16.1 decades = 6.09e-06
  QED3 large N, singlet fermion vs bare Maxwell (4 - d)                    z = 1.0000: factor over 16.1 decades = 8.20e-17
  GN large N, nonsinglet, N=4 (16/(15 pi^2 N), derived)                    z = 0.0270: factor over 16.1 decades = 3.68e-01
  weakly coupled 4D, gamma ~ 2 alpha/pi at alpha=1/128                     z = 0.0050: factor over 16.1 decades = 8.32e-01
  4D strongly coupled CFT, z = Delta(T1-T2) - 4 (BPS-type, model-dependent) z = 0.5000: factor over 16.1 decades = 9.05e-09
  same, z = 1                                                              z = 1.0000: factor over 16.1 decades = 8.20e-17
  same, z = 2                                                              z = 2.0000: factor over 16.1 decades = 6.72e-33

== (c) F2 initial split delta0 = c_e - c_gamma = -8.55e-3 at a^-1 = M_Pl ==
  gamma -> e+e- (LHAASO 1.4 PeV), lattice sign           : bound 2.7e-19 at 1.4e+06 GeV (12.94 decades): QED log flow gives 7.34e-03 (miss x2.8e+16); power law needs z >= 1.28
  IceCube PeV neutrinos (nu vs gamma), either sign       : bound 1.0e-20 at 1.0e+06 GeV (13.09 decades): QED log flow gives 7.33e-03 (miss x7.3e+17); power law needs z >= 1.37
  UHECR p vacuum Cherenkov (c_p > c_gamma) at 1e20 eV    : bound 4.4e-23 at 1.0e+11 GeV (8.09 decades): QED log flow gives 7.78e-03 (miss x1.8e+20); power law needs z >= 2.51
  gamma -> p pbar (c_gamma > c_p) at 1.4 PeV             : bound 9.0e-13 at 1.4e+06 GeV (12.94 decades): QED log flow gives 7.34e-03 (miss x8.2e+09); power law needs z >= 0.77
  GW170817 (c_g vs c_gamma, 3e-15): not reachable by any matter-sector flow; see (d)

== (d) graviton TT stiffness and speed ==
  canonical h_c = M_Pl h/2: mass term mu_TT h^2 = (4 mu_TT/M_Pl^2) h_c^2 -> m_g^2 ~ mu_TT/M_Pl^2 (dimension-2 coefficient)
  growth of (m_g/E)^2 from E = M_Pl to E = 1 TeV: x1.5e+32
  growth of (m_g/E)^2 from E = M_Pl to E = ~1e-15 eV (LIGO band, 100 Hz ~ 4e-13 eV order): x1.5e+86
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-01 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^0.0: 1.0e-04  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-04 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-03 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^0.0: 1.0e-12  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-12 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-01 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^0.5: 3.2e-05  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 3e-05 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-03 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^0.5: 3.2e-14  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 3e-14 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-01 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^1.0: 1.0e-05  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-05 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-03 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^1.0: 1.0e-15  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-15 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-01 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^2.0: 1.0e-06  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-06 untouched
  stiffness share from modes below 1e-03 Lambda with LV profile (k/Lambda)^2.0: 1.0e-18  -> flow can remove at most this share; UV share 1 - 1e-18 untouched
  graviton-speed pull from 100 matter dof (Sakharov-type estimate): integrated rate 0.053 -> suppression factor >= 0.949 (GW170817 needs 3e-15/8.5e-3 = 4e-13)
  graviton-speed pull from 1000 matter dof (Sakharov-type estimate): integrated rate 0.528 -> suppression factor >= 0.590 (GW170817 needs 3e-15/8.5e-3 = 4e-13)
  h anomalous dimension from matter at scale mu ~ c_T mu^2/M_Pl^2: at 1 TeV ~ (1e3/1.22e19)^2 = 6.7e-33 x c_T -> cannot turn the dimension-2 mass into an irrelevant operator
